<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ivan III</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ivan III was Grand Prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> in the late fifteenth century, often called Ivan the Great. He unified much of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> under Moscow, annexed Novgorod and ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatar</a> overlordship after the stand on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ugra-river">Ugra River</a> in 1480. His reign laid the foundations of the Russian state that became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ivan-iii.jpg" alt="Ivan III" width="316" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ivan_III_of_Russia_3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
